; worldsheet.eval - the character sheet, two things about it (WorldTest phase 21).
;
; IT IS NOT A PAUSE (Michael, 2026-09-28): only the pause menu and the editor's
; pause button stop the game. Brand is poisoned, his sheet opened, and twenty
; FRAMES pass with it open - plain `state` lines, one a frame, at 100x time.
; `step` would not do: it advances the world directly, whatever the app state,
; and so passes whether the sheet pauses or not. His health must fall while the
; page is up. How far is not the point and depends on how long a headless frame
; takes (under a millisecond); that it moves at all is, since a frozen world
; prints the same number twice.
;
; IT CLOSES TO WHERE IT WAS OPENED FROM, even after paging through the party
; with < and > (after > the close box used to do nothing). `sheet <n>` goes
; through the same OpenCharacterSheet the portrait click and the < > buttons
; use, and `sheet off` through the close box's own resume. In a level first,
; then out on the world map, where a wrong resume would drop a travelling party
; into whatever level was last loaded.
logecho on
reset
effect poison 0 3 60
party
sheet 0
timescale 100
state
state
state
state
state
state
state
state
state
state
state
state
state
state
state
state
state
state
state
state
timescale 1
party
sheet off
sheet 0
sheet 1
sheet 2
sheet off
state
leave
sheet 0
sheet 1
sheet off
state
